From 0ef7884e3871f12a50104a265100585e23c645cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 23:38:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 464/468] AOSCOS: net: stmmac: dwmac-phytium: drop stale
 lpi_irq assignment

The Phytium 6.6-based dwmac-phytium glue assigns stmmac_res.lpi_irq, but
upstream removed the lpi_irq member from struct stmmac_resources along
with lpi_intr_o support ("net: stmmac: remove support for lpi_intr_o",
14eb64db8ff0, present in the v7.3-rc1 base), so the assignment no longer
compiles. Drop it; the Phytium GMAC has no LPI interrupt to describe.
This resurrects a change originally carried in-tree by Icenowy Zheng in
the previous copy of the GMAC glue pick, which was lost when the pick
was refreshed from the Phytium source.

Fixes: "BACKPORT: PHYTIUM: net: stmmac: Add Phytium GMAC glue layer"

Not verified by a full kernel build.

This commit is authored with assistance from AI/LLM:
- Model: Kimi k3 (kimi-code/k3)
- Platform: Kimi Code (https://www.kimi.com)
- Agent platform: Kimi Code CLI (https://github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-cli)
- Prompt: In c93b9dceb96210626f58780dfb151de10961f674, Icenowy Zheng
  removed lpi_irq without explaination, and this change got lost during
  our re-pick. Investigate what's the rationale behind this change, and
  if it's still needed, split into a separate AOSCOS: patch.

Assisted-by: Kimi-k3
Signed-off-by: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-phytium.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-phytium.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-phytium.c
index 11fdd4eab9c1d..3c19f21270419 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-phytium.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-phytium.c
@@ -193,7 +193,6 @@ static int phytium_dwmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ENXIO;
 	}
 	stmmac_res.wol_irq = stmmac_res.irq;
-	stmmac_res.lpi_irq = -1;
 
 	return  stmmac_dvr_probe(&pdev->dev, plat, &stmmac_res);
 }
